        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-31T09:31:15+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-31T09:31:15+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T00:01:15Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T00:01:15Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system southeast of SA continues extending a ridge across the state, as it moves over Victoria and into the Tasman Sea by late Monday. A cold front is then forecast to move across the state on Tuesday, as another ridge and high push in behind the front on Wednesday. Another cold front may slip across the southeast parts of SA early Thursday, with the high moving over eastern SA.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
            </forecast-period>
